# Vulnerability details


## Impact

The `withdrawStake` function relies on the `isValidUnbondingLock` function to validate ownership of unbonding locks. However, this dependency on external validation poses a critical security risk. The `withdrawStake` function does not explicitly verify if the caller is the owner of the specified unbonding lock. This lack of direct access control allows an attacker to potentially perform unauthorized withdrawals. Furthermore, the function checks if the `withdrawRound` of the unbonding lock is before or equal to the current round to determine the validity of the withdrawal. While this check is essential, it alone may not be sufficient to prevent unauthorized withdrawals, especially if an attacker manipulates the `withdrawRound.`

## Proof of Concept

**[withdrawStake](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-08-livepeer/blob/bcf493b98d0ef835e969e637f25ea51ab77fabb6/contracts/bonding/BondingManager.sol#L249-L268) function's logic**

